  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure off the New England coast will allow for dry\nweather to continue today into much of the day on Thursday.\nSoutherly return flow will allow for high temperatures to warm\ninto the 70s, well above normal for late October. High\ntemperatures may challenge record highs for Thursday, see\nclimate section below for more information. \n\nA cold front will enter the region from the northwest Thursday\nevening accompanied by weak forcing aloft. Latest hi-res \nguidance has increased precipitation chances across Northwest \nOhio though the highest chances (40-60%) remain localized to \nNortheast Ohio and Northwest Pennsylvania. \n\nHigh pressure returns Friday into Saturday allowing for another\nwindow of dry weather. Temperatures will be slightly cooler, but\nremain above normal with highs in the 60s and lows in the 40s\nand 50s. \n\nThe weather pattern takes a turn Sunday into next \nweek with rain chances returning Sunday. Rain chances look to \nlinger into next week.",
